This component is part of the data processing pipeline, primarly responsible for data normalization with parser classes (ExcelDataParser, JSONDataParser) and integration using DataSourceAdapter. The DataListener interface defines how listening to data streams starts and stops, allowing different data sources to be handled in a uniform way.
The parsers convert raw input data (CSV or JSON strings) into a standardized format by transforming it into a list of IncomingDataPoint objects, which contain the same attributes as a patient record. During this process, invalid/incomplete/broken records are filtered out.
The ExcelDataParser is responsible for parsing raw CSV data: It splits the raw input string into lines, filters out invalid or incomplete records, and converts valid entries into standardized IncomingDataPoint objects.
The JSONDataParser is responsible for parsing JSON type data: It also uses line by line processing and filters out invalid or incomplete records, then converts valid entries into standardized IncomingDataPoint objects.
The DataSourceAdapter integrates these normalized data points into the system. For each incoming data point it creates a record and adds it to the correct patient, if the patient exists, if not, then (not in the DataSourceAdapter) a patient will be created in another module, and the created record will be added to the patient. 
